- op: discuss  # 2402
  at: '2026-08-25T07:27:48Z'  # 2402
  by: agent  # 2402
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2402
  clock: 4  # 2402
  nonce: '2402'  # 2402
  message: "SATISFIED 2026-08-25. INV-bokim and INV-pogob are ONE defect seen from two\nsides and are closed by ONE fix; both threads carry this entry.\n\nTHE SHAPE, restated once. Two predicates answered \"does this file announce\nitself as generated\", they disagreed, and the MORE DESTRUCTIVE consumer held\nthe WEAKER rule: is_likely_minified heuristic 3 was an unanchored\ncase-insensitive (Generated by|@generated|DO NOT EDIT) over five lines and it\ndecides Tier.DERIVED, which drops EVERY SYMBOL IN THE FILE, while the\ncomment-anchored _GENERATED_HEADER_PATTERN only set the is_generated flag.\n_classify_file_core consults the loose one at step 2 and returns immediately.\n\nBOTH FILED REPROS RE-RUN AT TIP BEFORE THE FIX, each with its control:\n  py 'regenerated by' docstring : loose=True   strict=False\n  py plain docstring            : loose=False  strict=False   <- CONTROL\n  go '// generated by ...'      : loose=True   strict=False\n  go '// leading comment'       : loose=False  strict=False   <- CONTROL\n\nTHE UNION IS THE RULE, NOT THE STRICT SET -- and finding that out is why this\nis not a two-line change. Collapsing onto _GENERATED_HEADER_PATTERN as it stood\nwould have LOST a real detection: the Python protobuf compiler writes\n\"# Generated by the protocol buffer compiler.  DO NOT EDIT!\", which is not\n\"Code generated by\". The shared rule is comment-anchored and keeps the weak\nphrase \"generated by\" ONLY where DO NOT EDIT co-occurs on the same line.\n\nTHE SCOPE IS THE LEADING COMMENT BLOCK, and a first cut got that wrong in a way\nonly measurement caught. Anchoring but scanning the whole 4 KiB head passed\nevery unit test and newly classified three FIRST-PARTY files as generated on a\nfive-repo sweep:\n    test_max_tier.py:106              # ...via its \"DO NOT EDIT\" header,\n    BaseToggleActionDelegate.java:38  // TODO Auto-generated method stub\n    CloverModuleConfig.java:41        // autogenerated\nThe first is INV-bokim's own defect wearing a comment instead of a docstring.\nThe second is Eclipse's per-METHOD stub marker, which says nothing about the\nfile. It must be the BLOCK and not the first five lines, because a real\ndeclaration routinely sits under a licence notice -- http4s MimeDB.scala\ncarries \"// Autogenerated file, don't edit\" at line 17 under 15 lines of\nApache, and IS generated. All three are pinned as regressions with the\nlicence-header case as the control.\n\nA/B OVER SIX REPOSITORIES, 14,114 scanned files, after the scope fix:\n  4 files STOP being Tier.DERIVED -- symbols recovered:\n      hypergumbo test_spec_linker_count.py and test_scip_generated.py --\n        INV-bokim's OWN two, now FIRST_PARTY alongside the test_ir.py control\n      hypergumbo SECURITY.md\n      clover GlobalCoverageRecordingTranscript.java (\"previously generated by\n        an instrumenter\" -- javadoc prose on a hand-written class)\n  1 file NEWLY Tier.DERIVED:\n      http4s MimeDB.scala -- genuinely generated\n  caddy, VernissageServer, keycloak (8,896 files): NO CHANGE AT ALL\n\nThe two consumers now agree on every file, which is the property INV-pogob was\nfiled for.\n\nRESIDUAL, STATED. A block comment whose interior lines carry no prefix of their\nown (a bare /* followed by unprefixed prose) ends the block at that line, so a\nmarker below it is missed. Deliberate, pinned by a test, and it errs toward\nKEEPING symbols -- the direction INV-bokim was filed about.\n\nShipped in the same PR; evidence in ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/campaign_p0_08252026/."  # 2402
